ive to her.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: That's a great idea. Look at this. Western College has had a program in journalism for two years now.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You should tell her about the program.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Here's what it says:", "id": 1, "image": "engenn7le15ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"time": "23500", "text": "The ability to tell compelling stories has always been the backbone of journalism.  At Western College, we have been working hard to create a program that surpasses your expectations.  Our graduates have told us again and again how much they love this program.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le15ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "39000", "text": "You can choose one area to concentrate on. You could focus on the area that interests you the most: print, broadcast or radio journalism, or technical studies.  If you choose print journalism, you'll learn the skills necessary to get to the heart of every story you write.  If you opt for broadcast journalism, you'll develop the confidence to shine in front of the camera. If you select radio journalism, you'll develop the abilities needed to communicate with your audience only using your voice.  If you want to explore the technical side of journalism, you'll develop the skills to operate cameras and edit footage.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le15ob06re2img02.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le15ob06re2img05.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 2, "_data": [], "title": ""}]}]}